Nothing in section 111 shall operate so as to render unlawful or invalid any payment of wages by the employer to the employee with the employee’s written consent in any of the following ways:
(a) payment into an account at a bank or a finance company licensed under the Banking and Financial Institutions Act 1989 [Act 372] in any part of Sarawak being an account in the name of the employee or an account in the name of the employee jointly with one or more other person, not being his employer;
